/* The Turkish peer. It duplicates the `NSAlarmKitUsageDescription` value `project.yml` writes into
   `App/Info.plist`, and it has to: the plist value is the base — the fallback for a locale that is
   neither Turkish nor English — but a value in `Info.plist` alone is not a *localization*. Measured
   on the built bundle: with `en.lproj` as the only `.lproj`, `Bundle.preferredLocalizations` answers
   `["en"]` even for a `tr-TR` device, so a Turkish phone would have read the English sentence. With
   both files present it answers `["tr"]` for `tr-TR`, `["en"]` for `en-US`, and `["tr"]` for
   anything else — which is spec §6.4 exactly. Edit the three together. */
"NSAlarmKitUsageDescription" = "İlaç hatırlatmalarınızın tam ekran alarm olarak çalabilmesi için Salus'un alarm iznine ihtiyacı var.";

/* iOS-M8, the app lock's Face ID prompt. The same three-places rule as above: this repeats the base
   value `project.yml` writes into `App/Info.plist`, because a value in `Info.plist` alone is not a
   *localization* and a `tr-TR` device would otherwise read the English peer. */
"NSFaceIDUsageDescription" = "Uygulama kilidini açmak için Salus'un Face ID iznine ihtiyacı var.";
